      en: "The Şahbuz State Nature Reserve was established in 2003 in the Nakhchivan Autonomous Republic. It is located in a high-altitude alpine region and includes the picturesque Batabat Lake with its famous floating peat island. The main goal of the reserve is to protect the pristine water resources, rich mountain flora, and rare animal species of the region. The area is known for its medicinal plants and mineral springs. The landscape is characterized by subalpine meadows, rock formations, and mountain lakes. The reserve is an important habitat for brown bears, bezoar goats, and a variety of bird species. It also serves as an important research center for the study of mountain ecosystems."
